        "One month passed, then another. Just before New Year, Ivan's brother-in-law came to town and stayed with them. Ivan was at the law courts, and Praskovya Fedorovna had gone shopping. When Ivan came home and entered his study, he found his brother-in-law there, a healthy, red-faced man, unpacking his own portmanteau. The brother-in-law heard Ivan's footsteps, raised his head, and looked at him for a moment without saying anything. That look told Ivan everything. His brother-in-law opened his mouth as if he were about to cry out in surprise, then stopped himself. That restraint confirmed it.",
        "\"I have changed, haven't I?\"",
        "\"Yes, there is a change.\"",
        "After that, no matter how Ivan tried to make him return to the subject of his appearance, the brother-in-law would not say anything more. Praskovya Fedorovna came home, and her brother went out to speak with her. Ivan locked the door and examined himself in the mirror, first full face, then in profile. He picked up a photograph of himself with his wife and compared the photograph with what he saw in the glass. The change was enormous. Then he bared his arms to the elbow, looked at them, pulled his sleeves down again, sat on an ottoman, and grew blacker than night.",
